0,Colonia Tovar dialect - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colonia_Tovar_dialect,"The Colonia Tovar dialect, or Alemán Coloniero, is a dialect that is spoken in Colonia Tovar, Venezuela, and belongs to the Low Alemannic branch of German.","German, Colonia Tovar",Indo-European
1,Colonia Tovar - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colonia_Tovar,"Colonia Tovar (Tovar Colony) is a mountain town of Venezuela, capital of the municipality Tovar in Aragua state. It is located about 65.5 km (41 mi) west of Caracas.","German, Colonia Tovar",Indo-European
2,"German, Colonia Tovar Language (GCT) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/gct/,Colonia Tovar German is an endangered indigenous language of Venezuela. It belongs to the Indo-European language family. The language is used as a first language by adults only. It is not known to be taught in schools.,"German, Colonia Tovar",Indo-European
3,"Wait, There’s a Little Slice of Germany in Venezuela? Here’s the ...",https://nuestrostories.com/2025/01/wait-theres-a-little-slice-of-germany-in-venezuela-heres-the-fascinating-story-of-colonia-tovar/,"Atmospheric restaurants sell sausages and sauerkraut served by staff in traditional German clothes, and bakeries proudly display Black Forest cake with decadent layers of chocolate, cherries and cream. While this might sound like a wholesome German mountain town, this isn’t Germany. It’s the Venezuelan mountain town of Colonia Tovar.","German, Colonia Tovar",Indo-European
4,"Celebrations start at Caribbean's Germany, Colonia Tovar",https://www.dailysabah.com/life/celebrations-start-at-caribbeans-germany-colonia-tovar/news,"Alpine folk music echoes in Colonia Tovar, the German enclave in Venezuela that is frozen in time, accompanying the bright-red harlequin costumes worn for the carnival celebrations. ...","German, Colonia Tovar",Indo-European
5,Colonia Tovar: A German Town in Venezuela - Culinistanbul,https://culinistanbul.com/colonia-tovar-a-german-town-in-venezuela/,"Today, April 8 is celebrated as the official founding day of Colonia Tovar, and every year the town comes alive with music, dance, traditional German food, and a festival atmosphere that feels unlike anywhere else in Venezuela.","German, Colonia Tovar",Indo-European
6,Colonia Tovar dialect — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Colonia_Tovar_dialect,"The Colonia Tovar dialect, also known as Alemán Coloniero, is a variety of Low Alemannic German preserved in the Venezuelan town of Colonia Tovar by descendants of approximately 400 immigrants from the Grand Duchy of Baden who arrived in 1843 to establish an agricultural colony in the Andean region. [1] [2] This settlement, promoted by Venezuelan authorities to exploit fertile lands near ...","German, Colonia Tovar",Indo-European
7,Colonia Tovar — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Colonia_Tovar,"Colonia Tovar was founded on April 8, 1843, by a group of approximately 390 German immigrants from the Grand Duchy of Baden, particularly the Kaiserstuhl region near the Black Forest. [1][7] This settlement was the first major European colonization project in Venezuela, initiated under the administration of President José Antonio Páez to ...","German, Colonia Tovar",Indo-European
8,"Venezuela’s Little Germany, Colonia Tovar",https://thetravelersbuddy.com/colonia-tovar-venezuela/,"Nestled in the Venezuelan mountains, Colonia Tovar offers a unique slice of German culture and architecture. It’s a town that blends traditional German customs with Venezuelan charm. Colonia Tovar, often referred to as “Venezuela’s little Germany,” is a picturesque town located in the Aragua state, approximately 70 kilometers west of ...","German, Colonia Tovar",Indo-European
